#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0659 expect=violation domain=QS
#note "S1 (2026-09-14): the pin moved from variable_name to the RESOLVED column, because the Check moved from varname() per-variable iteration to var_exists(\"--EVAL\") / var_exists(\"--EVALID\"). The -- prefix resolves to the current domain, so this rule can no longer cross-match a foreign-domain column (a stray FTEVAL in a QS dataset used to satisfy the old hard-coded membership list). QSEVAL is declared in a QS dataset. Since the group-P varname() rewrite (D-15, 2026-09-12) the Check is the per-variable membership test varname() in [QSEVAL, FTEVAL] with Output_Variables [variable_name], so the finding is pinned by the culprit's NAME rather than by a row. Modelled on the retired CORE-family twin's suite, whose post-rewrite Check was byte-identical."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 nameOnly=QSEVAL
dataset QS label=Questionnaires
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col QSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col QSEVAL   type=Char label="Evaluator"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | QS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | INVESTIGATOR
